@module level3data ; Level 3
@about The level's body: the header the game reads at $C4AE, the sprites, the object table, the metatiles, the map, the wave script, the enemy kinds and their movement scripts, the two mover tables and the movers.
$C4AE b L3Header ; The level header: restart point, checkpoints and the pointers the game reads
> Restart column $00, restart wave $0000; checkpoint columns $00, $FF, $FF with wave entries $E856, $EA31, $EA31; objects $DD8E, map $E716, kinds $ED50, movers $F0A6 and $F0C6.
$C4AF L3RestartWave ; the wave entry a life restarts at (the game keeps its live copy here)
$C4B1 L3Checks ; three checkpoint columns (CheckRestart)
$C4B4 L3WaveStarts ; the wave entries of the start and the checkpoints
$C4BA L3Pointers ; objects, map, kinds, movers 1, movers 2
$C4C4 b L3Spare ; zeros up to the sprites
$C4E0 b L3Sprites 9 ; The level's sprites: cells of 9 bytes (attribute, 8 pixel bytes) the object table points at
@res levels/level3/sprites.bin
$DD8E b L3Objects 4 ; The level's object table: width, height, the cells' address (LevelObject)
@res levels/level3/objects.bin
$DF36 b L3Metatiles 9 ; The metatiles, 144 bytes each (4 x 4 cells of 9 bytes), numbered down from the map: metatile n at $E716 - 144 x (n + 1) (MetatileAddress); 14 of them
@res levels/level3/metatiles.bin
$E716 b L3Map 5 ; The map: 5 bytes a block column (64 columns), each byte a metatile (bits 0-5) and its drawer (bits 6-7)
@res levels/level3/map.bin
$E856 b L3Waves ; The wave script: entries (scroll position, kind, script) RunWaves starts; then the enemies' movement scripts
$ED50 b L3Kinds ; The enemy kinds StartWave reads (LevelKinds)
$F0A6 w L3MoversA ; The first mover of each kind (16 words, LevelMoves)
$F0C6 w L3MoversB ; The second mover of each kind (16 words, LevelMoves2)
